  Based on the app's current feature set, here are natural premium candidates organised by category:

Core Workout Features
Superset creation — linking exercises is a power-user feature
Multiple active workout plans — free tier gets 1 plan, premium gets unlimited
Custom rest timer sounds — free gets default beep, premium gets more options
Workout color themes — free gets 4–5 basic colors, premium gets full palette
Add/remove sets during active workout — keep basic tracking free, editing is advanced
Planning & Scheduling
Cycle length limit — free capped at e.g. 180-day cycles, premium unlimited
Workout history beyond 30/90 days — archive access is a classic paywall
Export workout data (CSV/JSON) — data portability as premium perk
Progress & Analytics
Full progress dashboard — charts, trends, streaks beyond basic stats
Weight & calorie correlation chart — already exists, easy to gate
Exercise progress graphs — per-exercise volume/PR tracking over time
Calendar with color dots — the view you just built
Nutrition
Meal templates — free gets e.g. 3 templates, premium unlimited
Custom foods — free gets e.g. 10, premium unlimited
Import / Integration
FitNotes CSV import — data migration is a premium hook
Future: Apple Health / Google Fit sync
Recommended free/premium split
Free Premium
1 active plan, 7-day cycle Unlimited plans & cycles
3 meal templates Unlimited templates
30-day history Full history + export
Basic progress (weight chart) Full analytics dashboard
Manual food search Barcode scanner + online DB
Standard colors Full color palette
The strongest paywalls tend to be barcode scanning, unlimited plans, and full analytics — these are features users feel the value of immediately and justify a subscription.
